{
  "description": "Firmware releases and updates over the air (protocol/firmware-update.md, decisions FU3-*). Checked by the shared Python (controller/atalaia_controller/firmware_release.py: the site server's catalogue, the controller, tools/firmware_release.py) and the Field Box's C side (firmware/esp32/main/fw_update.c with Monocypher; firmware/esp32/test/firmware_vectors.h, made by tools/protogen.py). rfc8032: the five Ed25519 test vectors of RFC 8032 section 7.1, copied from the RFC. signing_key is TEST 1's key and other_key TEST 2's: public test keys, never release keys. releases: manifests signed with signing_key (Ed25519 is deterministic: any RFC 8032 implementation makes the same signatures), each with the release text a box fetches; valid ones verify with signing_key alone, invalid ones fail for their reason. release_texts_invalid: texts a box must refuse before any signature check. versions: semver_order is Semantic Versioning 2.0.0's own example; the rest pin this project's rule (firmware.py's VERSION). images: the first 324 bytes of an image (ESP-IDF image and segment headers, esp_app_desc_t, the Atalaia descriptor). reports: a box's report and its HMAC-SHA256 with the game key.",
